# Build output
/target
**/target
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key material. Nothing here may ever reach a commit.
#
# *.plnekey alone was not enough: the wallet writes whatever name --out is
# given, and this project's own README says
#
#     plaine-wallet new --role spend --out miner.key --no-passphrase
#
# so following the quick-start inside a checkout leaves an unignored private
# key in the working tree - and with `kdf: none` that file holds the seed in
# the clear. The passphrase sources README documents (pass.txt,
# --passphrase-file) are the same hazard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.key
*.plnekey
*.key.journal
*.plnekey.journal
pass.txt
passphrase.txt
passphrase*.txt
*.seed
*.backup
# The one exception: key files written by upstream's wallet from a published test
# seed, so the tests can prove old files still open. See its README; nothing real.
!wallet/tests/fixtures/*.plnekey

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node state. Written into --data-dir, which defaults elsewhere but is often
# pointed at a folder inside the checkout while testing. chain.redb and the
# segment files reach gigabytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
noded.toml
# ...except the settings file the release archives ship.
!scripts/release/noded.toml
noded.lock
peers.dat
chain.redb
LOCK
/segments/
**/segments/
*.redb

# Miner
miner.json

# Logs
*.log

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.rustfmt.toml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Release archives, built by scripts/package-release.sh.
dist/
